const bodyHtml = `<p>The villages behind Cannes — Mougins, Valbonne, Biot, Mouans-Sartoux, Roquefort-les-Pins, Châteauneuf — are where most of my in-home sessions happen, because that's where the international families live: ten minutes from Mougins School, the International School of Nice and the CIV at Valbonne, twenty from Sophia Antipolis, forty from the airport. All of it is included in the travel area. €180 for 45 minutes at your home, in English, Russian or Ukrainian.</p>
<p>I'm twenty minutes away for most of these villages and same-day is often possible.</p>
<h2>Where sessions happen in Mougins &amp; Valbonne</h2><p><strong>Villas.</strong> Mougins village and the roads towards the golf courses, Valbonne village and the Sophia side, Biot above the glassworks, Mouans-Sartoux, Roquefort, Châteauneuf, Opio, Plascassier. A bedroom with the shutters down against the afternoon — the pines and the pool pump the only sound.</p>
<p><strong>Sophia Antipolis.</strong> Early evening at home after the last call, or at my space in Cannes on the way past.</p>
<p><strong>Grasse, Vence, the higher villages.</strong> On request, with a small travel addition.</p>
<h2>Who comes, and for what</h2><p>Parents holding a household in a second language while the children settle into a school where half the class is also new. Professionals at Sophia who work in English all day and are braced by 7 pm. Families in their first September here, when the household's nervous system sets its default for the year. And — this is the one I'd underline — the parent who is doing everything right and is closer to empty than they'll say.</p>
<h2>What a session is</h2><p>Forty-five minutes lying on your back, fully clothed. Hands resting lightly on or just above the body from head to feet, in a set sequence. No conversation during, nothing to believe, nothing to do. Most people drop into deep rest within ten minutes; many fall asleep. At the end I let you lie for a moment, then leave you to it. Sleep that night is usually the first thing people notice.</p>
<h2>Mougins &amp; Valbonne, specifically</h2><p>Timing here is about the school day. Drop-off is 8:30, pickup around 4. A session at 10 or at 2 fits inside that window with time to sleep afterwards, which most parents do. Children's sessions, shorter and gentler, can follow at bedtime the same day — always alongside the paediatrician, and usually after the parent has had a few first. There's a longer piece on how sessions work for expat families, and one on the villages specifically.</p>
